\ Temporary bridge from a native signed CAL day into an exact
\ signed-wide day. The destination is a wide signed day record.
\ The native minimum -2147483648 cannot be negated within a signed
\ 32-bit number, so this bridge refuses that one input explicitly.
\ The full calendar still uses the stricter temporary safety bounds.
\ Arbitrary-wide dates do not pass through this bridge.

The converted wide signed day is a wide signed day.
The native to wide conversion succeeded is a number.

To convert a calendar day into a wide signed day:
  Put 0 into the native to wide conversion succeeded.
  If the calendar day is less than -2147483647, exit.
  Put the calendar day into an absolute calendar day.
  Put 1 into a native day polarity number.
  If the absolute calendar day is less than 0,
    multiply -1 by the absolute calendar day;
    put -1 into the native day polarity number.
  Convert the absolute calendar day to a string.
  Put the string into a native day magnitude wide quantity.
  Set the converted wide signed day from the native day magnitude wide quantity given the native day polarity number.
  Put 1 into the native to wide conversion succeeded.
